The SEP engine implements a quantum-inspired pattern processing system with three core components:

## Quantum Pattern Processing
- Pattern evolution through quantum manifolds with coherence modulation
- Quantum binary state analysis (QBSA) for pattern stability detection 
- Pattern mutation based on quantum fourier hierarchy (QFH)
- Coherence-based validation using stability thresholds

Key files:
- src/quantum/quantum_processor.cpp
- src/quantum/pattern_evolution.cpp
- include/quantum/qbsa.h

## Memory Management 
- Three-tier memory hierarchy (STM/MTM/LTM)
- Coherence-based promotion/demotion between tiers
- Pattern relationship tracking through quantum entanglement
- Redis-based persistence for long-term memory

Key files:
- src/memory/memory_tier_manager.cpp
- src/memory/quantum_coherence_manager.cpp
- include/memory/types.h

## API Integration
- Pattern processing API with coherence validation
- Memory tier status reporting and management
- Quantum state evolution control interface
- Integration with Blender for pattern visualization
- Audio pipeline for pattern generation from sound

Key files:
- src/api/server.cpp
- src/api/bridge.cpp
- include/api/sep_engine.h

The system operates on quantum-inspired principles where patterns evolve through stability states based on coherence metrics. Memory management uses a hierarchical approach with promotion/demotion based on pattern stability and relationships. The API layer provides interfaces for pattern processing, visualization and audio integration.

